{"Title":"An Act relative to protecting coastal communities","BillNumber":"H862","DocketNumber":"HD382","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"L_M1","Name":"Lenny Mirra","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T15:07:20.747"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"L_M1","Name":"Lenny Mirra","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T15:07:20.7466667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H862/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Mirra of Georgetown, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 862) of Lenny Mirra relative to protecting coastal communities.  Environment and Natural Resources.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 40 of Chapter 131 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word \"section\", in line 493, the following:- “provided, that when establishing such regulations, the commissioner shall permit the construction of a coastal engineering structure, as defined by 310 CMR 10.23, on coastal dunes when an emergency or exigent situation occurs, as determined by the commissioner.” \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}